TITLE:: Domifare
summary:: A live coding language for music that is entered by playing or singing commands in solresol.
categories:: Live Coding, Libraries/Domifare

DESCRIPTION::
A live coding language,modelled on ixilang, that is designed for instrumentalists. The GUI is optiised for
tuba, but it should work for other kinds of players also.

Under nromal conditions, the user would not use any of the instance methods, but instead control the
object/language via pitch-based input.


CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a new instance of Domifare, ready to run. This boots the server.

ARGUMENT:: server
An optional Server argument. If noneis provided, it uses Server.default

ARGUMENT:: clock
An optional TempoClock or ExternalClock. If none is provided, it creates a clock.

ARGUMENT:: dur
An optional duration for loops. If none is provided, it calculates one from the clock. If the clock and the dur do not divide evenly, the clock is adjusted.



INSTANCEMETHODS::



METHOD:: gui
Open the GUI. You will need to resize the GUI window.

ARGUMENT:: parent
Optional if you want the GUI in an existing window

ARGUMENT:: bounds
Optional if you want the GUI in an existing window



EXAMPLES::

code::
d = Domifare(s);
d.gui;
::
